Z||000024||PIPO||08-10-2001||09:39 AM||||Hi friends!<BR>Now I have more promising news. IT SEEMS that the german FIEROLUKE is rigth (see post 06-20-2001).<BR>I was present in this test yesterday: My current repair men take the outer case of the ECM out and reconected the bare printed circuit board. Therefore, all electronic components were visible. Then I started engine. He shows me that by pushing down one end of the EPROM the engine stops. This does not occurred by pressing any other component. This also occurs by a slight twisting or warping of the printed board in the terminals area, which is close to the EPROM mounting base. The EPROM is pressure mounted on a fixed base, which in turn is soldered to the printed circuit board. The EPROM is labeled “7901142 TBE Philippines”. You do not see any damage, even with a magnifying glass. Yes, the circuit is protected with a transparent coating.<BR>Now I need to find somebody able to find the electrical path cut, and fix the problem. I cross my fingers.<BR>Any additional comment will be appreciated.<BR>Pipo <BR>||||reg||11
Z||000025||maryjane||08-10-2001||11:30 AM||||if one of the wiring digrams in the back of the Haynes book will help, I'll scan it and email it. Anybody know which one he needs?||||reg||1
Z||000026||fieroluke||08-11-2001||05:50 AM||||I would definitely replace the ECM then.<BR>The damage on my board was also not visible, only after soldering many surface parts, one would no longer accept solder on one end. This was not visible at all, but unless you're experienced with electronics and soldering, I would recommend against doing this yourself. This ECM is not rare, but if you go to a junkyard, try to get one that has been "remanufactured", because GM has identified the problem and remanufactured ECMs have a better chance of being fault free. Otherwise you may end up with another faulty ECM with the fault on another part of the circuit board.<P>Best regards,<P>-Oliver<P>------------------<BR>Visit my website: <A HREF="http://www.fieros.de" TARGET=_blank>www.fieros.de</A>  for lots of technical and other Fiero related information<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fieros.de/jpg/mycars.jpg"> ||||reg||3
Z||000027||PIPO||09-15-2001||12:35 PM||||Hi people, again<BR>First of all let me condemn the coward attack suffered by newyorkers innocent civilians!!!<BR>Next, to the point: After many repairs and checks, the fail still subsists.<BR>Please help me: <BR>1. Where could I find a second hand ECM for my car, tested, CHEAP, and in good conditions?<BR>2. Can I save the main fiero chip or EPROM or something, and purchase just the basic stuff?<BR>3. Which are the cars-models-years that possess the same ECM, in order to look simultaneously for one here in Chile?<BR>Thanks in advance for your help.<BR>Pipo||||reg||8
